  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit (recorded as basis cash). Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (p4, Total Governmental Funds column); the statement rolls fund balances (287,128 -> 233,266), recorded as beginning/ending fund balance. Cash and investment fields null as in FY2024 (no single printed governmental cash total; cash and fund balance kept separate). Business-type lines from the modified cash proprietary statement (p6), which ties to the government-wide modified cash Statement of Activities (p2: charges 416,060, expenses 336,582, transfers (80,500), net position 80,875 -> 79,853); measure cash as in FY2024 (modified cash net position consists only of cash). The accrual-basis proprietary statements on pp8-10 (supplementary) are not used; proprietary is null for a cash-basis report. Detail: the only supplementary schedule is the combined all-fund-types Budgetary Comparison Schedule (p7), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds (p4) and proprietary funds (p6) statements; budget figures are all-funds only, so budget_final is null. Intergovernmental 59,826 split by the all-fund budget schedule's breakdown (p7: highway allocation 37,796, municipal equalization 12,609, motor vehicle fees 2,897, other intergovernmental 6,524; ties exactly), as in FY2024; the Street and Alley Fund's 53,302 split the same way in detail. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
